      "content": "but it didnt just feel like i was noticing it better. i actually noticed a pattern where the volatility spikes happened exactly when my breathing hit a certain cadence. it's like the algorithm's decision loops and my own neural processing essentially locked into the same frequency. if you look at the data for those specific seconds, the order cancellations and the liquidity shifts look almost... intentional, following a wave pattern. wouldn't you say it's plausible that a high-speed system could pick up on unintentional bio-signals or subconscious entrainment from someone staring at the screen for hours?",
